Installed `PillToaster` and `pillToast` (`@/components/ui/pill-toast`).

Render the toaster once, near the root:

```tsx
import { PillToaster } from "@/components/ui/pill-toast";

<PillToaster position="top-right" theme="system" />
```

Then call it from anywhere:

```tsx
import { pillToast } from "@/components/ui/pill-toast";

pillToast.success({ title: "Saved" });
pillToast.error({ title: "Upload failed", description: "The file is larger than 10 MB." });
pillToast.promise(save(), {
  loading: { title: "Saving" },
  success: { title: "Saved", description: "All changes are stored." },
  error: { title: "Save failed" },
});
```

A toast with a description opens on hover or keyboard focus. The stylesheet is rendered by the toaster (a React 19 hoisted `<style>`); no CSS import is needed. The state colors are `--pill-toast-state-success`, `-loading`, `-error`, `-warning`, `-info` and `-action`. The `-icons-lucide` and `-icons-phosphor` items use icon-library glyphs instead of the toast's own.

